      {
        "type": "application",
        "title": "What the Long Rehabilitation Teaches About Institutions",
        "content": "The Galileo affair is a case study in how powerful institutions revise themselves. Five generalizable lessons emerge. First, institutions revise after the cost of not revising becomes unbearable, not after they are persuaded they were wrong. By 1822 the Catholic Church faced rising secular science across Europe (Laplace's Mécanique Céleste 1799-1825, growing astronomical observatories, post-Napoleonic intellectual freedom); maintaining a ban on heliocentric astronomy was costing more in credibility than any doctrinal point gained. Second, revision happens in steps that protect institutional dignity. The Holy Office never said in 1822: 'Galileo was right and we were wrong.' It said: 'astronomy textbooks can now teach heliocentrism.' The doctrinal block was removed without explicit retraction. Third, the cleanup commissions can take a generation. JPII's 1981 study commission worked eleven years before its formal report. Fourth, the public 'apology' is often more nuanced than headlines suggest. JPII spoke of 'tragic mutual incomprehension' — not simple wrong. The press wrote 'Vatican apologizes to Galileo'; the actual address was more careful. Fifth, even centuries-late acknowledgments matter. The 1992 address gave permission for Catholic theologians and Catholic-school teachers to discuss the church's historical fallibility on natural questions. This permission has reshaped how Catholic seminaries teach the boundary between faith and science, and how scientists in Catholic universities understand their autonomy. A four-century process of self-revision, observed in detail, is one of the most useful things the history of science has to offer the present. Authority eventually corrects itself — but only after evidence has done the long work first.",
        "visual": {
          "type": "diagram",
          "svg": "<svg viewBox=\"0 0 1100 1100\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\"><rect width=\"1100\" height=\"1100\" fill=\"#1a1a2e\"/><text x=\"550\" y=\"70\" font-size=\"34\" fill=\"#ffd700\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">Five Lessons on Institutional Revision</text><text x=\"550\" y=\"115\" font-size=\"22\" fill=\"#9ca3af\" text-anchor=\"middle\">What the 359-year walk-back tells us</text><rect x=\"60\" y=\"180\" width=\"480\" height=\"160\" fill=\"#1a1a2e\" stroke=\"#10b981\" stroke-width=\"3\" rx=\"10\"/><text x=\"80\" y=\"220\" font-size=\"22\" fill=\"#10b981\" font-weight=\"bold\">1. Pressure, not persuasion</text><text x=\"80\" y=\"260\" font-size=\"18\" fill=\"#ffffff\">Institutions revise when not</text><text x=\"80\" y=\"290\" font-size=\"18\" fill=\"#ffffff\">revising costs more than admitting</text><text x=\"80\" y=\"320\" font-size=\"18\" fill=\"#ffffff\">error - 1822 followed Laplace</text><rect x=\"560\" y=\"180\" width=\"480\" height=\"160\" fill=\"#1a1a2e\" stroke=\"#6366f1\" stroke-width=\"3\" rx=\"10\"/><text x=\"580\" y=\"220\" font-size=\"22\" fill=\"#6366f1\" font-weight=\"bold\">2. Stepwise dignity</text><text x=\"580\" y=\"260\" font-size=\"18\" fill=\"#ffffff\">Revisions protect face -</text><text x=\"580\" y=\"290\" font-size=\"18\" fill=\"#ffffff\">remove the block first, admit</text><text x=\"580\" y=\"320\" font-size=\"18\" fill=\"#ffffff\">the error decades later</text><rect x=\"60\" y=\"360\" width=\"480\" height=\"160\" fill=\"#1a1a2e\" stroke=\"#f59e0b\" stroke-width=\"3\" rx=\"10\"/><text x=\"80\" y=\"400\" font-size=\"22\" fill=\"#f59e0b\" font-weight=\"bold\">3. Commissions take time</text><text x=\"80\" y=\"440\" font-size=\"18\" fill=\"#ffffff\">JPII's commission worked 11 yrs</text><text x=\"80\" y=\"470\" font-size=\"18\" fill=\"#ffffff\">A generation of careful</text><text x=\"80\" y=\"500\" font-size=\"18\" fill=\"#ffffff\">historical investigation</text><rect x=\"560\" y=\"360\" width=\"480\" height=\"160\" fill=\"#1a1a2e\" stroke=\"#8b5cf6\" stroke-width=\"3\" rx=\"10\"/><text x=\"580\" y=\"400\" font-size=\"22\" fill=\"#8b5cf6\" font-weight=\"bold\">4. Nuance, not headlines</text><text x=\"580\" y=\"440\" font-size=\"18\" fill=\"#ffffff\">Press: Vatican apologizes</text><text x=\"580\" y=\"470\" font-size=\"18\" fill=\"#ffffff\">Actual: tragic mutual</text><text x=\"580\" y=\"500\" font-size=\"18\" fill=\"#ffffff\">incomprehension</text><rect x=\"200\" y=\"540\" width=\"700\" height=\"160\" fill=\"#1a1a2e\" stroke=\"#ec4899\" stroke-width=\"3\" rx=\"10\"/><text x=\"220\" y=\"580\" font-size=\"22\" fill=\"#ec4899\" font-weight=\"bold\">5. Late acknowledgments still matter</text><text x=\"220\" y=\"620\" font-size=\"18\" fill=\"#ffffff\">1992 reshaped how Catholic seminaries teach the</text><text x=\"220\" y=\"650\" font-size=\"18\" fill=\"#ffffff\">faith-science boundary and licensed open historical</text><text x=\"220\" y=\"680\" font-size=\"18\" fill=\"#ffffff\">discussion of church fallibility on natural questions</text><rect x=\"100\" y=\"730\" width=\"900\" height=\"300\" fill=\"#1a1a2e\" stroke=\"#ffd700\" stroke-width=\"3\" rx=\"10\"/><text x=\"550\" y=\"785\" font-size=\"24\" fill=\"#ffd700\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">The deep lesson</text><text x=\"130\" y=\"850\" font-size=\"22\" fill=\"#ffffff\">Authority eventually corrects itself -</text><text x=\"130\" y=\"890\" font-size=\"22\" fill=\"#ffffff\">but only after evidence has done the long work first.</text><text x=\"130\" y=\"960\" font-size=\"20\" fill=\"#10b981\">Newton, Bradley, Bessel: the physics</text><text x=\"130\" y=\"990\" font-size=\"20\" fill=\"#10b981\">Anfossi, Pius VII, JPII: the doctrine</text></svg>",
          "caption": "Galileo's rehabilitation is the slowest, best-documented institutional reversal in the history of ideas."
        }
      }
